he\n   remaining entry order is preserved, and the capacity now reports 2.\n2. **Given** a cache with capacity 2 and 2 entries, **When** it is resized\n   to 5, **Then** no entry is evicted and the capacity now reports 5.\n3. **Given** any cache state, **When** a resize is requested with an\n   invalid capacity (non-integer, boolean, zero, negative), **Then**\n   `ValueError` is raised and all entries, tags, recency order, and the\n   previous capacity are unchanged.\n4. **Given** a cache that has entries, **When** it is shrunk to a smaller\n   capacity, **Then** evicted entries' tag memberships are removed exactly\n   as with LRU eviction (no stale tags).\n5. **Given** a surviving entry across a resize, **When** the resize\n   completes, **Then** the entry's stored state is preserved as-is (no\n   re-copying, no expiry recomputation — see Assumptions for the expiry\n   clarification note).\n\n---\n\n### Edge Cases\n\n- Bare string passed as `tags` (must be rejected, not treated as an\n  iterable of characters).\n- Tag iterable containing a non-string entry (rejected before any state\n  change).\n- Duplicate tags in one `put` call (stored once).\n- Replacing a key with the same value but different tags (old memberships\n  removed; recency refreshed).\n- Replacing a key with invalid tags after a prior valid put (state fully\n  preserved, including recency).\n- Eviction of a key, then re-put of the same key (no stale tag\n  memberships from the evicted incarnation).\n- `get` on a key that was invalidated or evicted (raises `KeyError`).\n- Capacity of 1 (every put evicts the previous entry).\n- `maxsize` given as `True`/`False` (rejected: booleans are excluded).\n- Mutating a returned deep copy or the original object (no cross-talk with\n  the cache).\n\n- Bulk invalidation with duplicate tags in the request (deduplicated\n  before matching; count is distinct removed keys).\n- Bulk invalidation `all` mode with an empty tag set (removes zero,\n  never every key — supersedes the old design note).\n- Bulk invalidation with a generator tag source (consumed exactly once;\n  on validation failure the cache is unchanged).\n- Resize to the same capacity (no-op; state unchanged).\n- Resize shrinking to exactly the current entry count (no eviction).\n- Resize with boolean/zero/negative/non-int capacity (rejected, state\n  preserved).\n- Growing then shrinking back (order and entries survive the round trip).\n## Requirements *(mandatory)*\n\n### Functional Requirements\n\n- **FR-001**: The system MUST expose a new `TaggedCache` type in\n  `cachetools.tagged` (module `src/cachetools/tagged.py`) constructed with a\n  single `maxsize` argument (R01/R03 scope).\n- **FR-002**: `put(key, value, tags=())` MUST insert or replace an entry;\n  keys MUST be hashable; values MUST be copied on input so later mutation\n  of the caller's object does not change the stored value (R01).\n- **FR-003**: `get(key)` MUST return a detached deep copy of the stored\n  value, or raise `KeyError` for a missing key; it MUST refresh the\n  entry's recency (R01/R02).\n- **FR-004**: `tags` MUST be a finite iterable of strings; the system MUST\n  deduplicate tags per entry; a bare string MUST be rejected as `tags` and\n  any non-string tag entry MUST raise `ValueError`, in both cases before\n  any existing state is changed (R01).\n- **FR-005**: `invalidate(tag)` MUST remove exactly the currently cached\n  entries carrying that tag and return the number removed (R02).\n- **FR-006**: Replacing an existing key MUST remove its old tag\n  memberships (R02).\n- **FR-007**: LRU eviction MUST remove the evicted entry's tag\n  memberships so later reuse of the same key is not affected by stale\n  state (R02).\n- **FR-008**: `get` MUST refresh LRU recency of the accessed entry (R02).\n- **FR-009**: `len(cache)` MUST count only live entries (R02).\n- **FR-010**: `maxsize` MUST be a positive integer; booleans MUST be\n  excluded; invalid values MUST raise `ValueError` (R03).\n- **FR-